###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The crystal test error of 2b+3b+EAM is stated only as 'down to 2 meV/atom', so it is not encoded. All other errors (learning curves, Fig. 6 per-class errors of the final tabGAP and GAPs) are figure-only.
# - tabGAP is named in the authors' earlier work (Ref. 9, byggmastar2021 in the corpus); its registry origin and any derivation from GAP wait for that paper. Short-range order parameters and Table I properties are properties.
# - The registry method GAP carries mlips:SOAPDescriptor (label 'GAP with SOAP kernel'), but the encoded GAP here uses 2b, 3b and EAM descriptors; the registry row is a legacy shared IRI and is flagged for review rather than changed here.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/byggmastar2022.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

